
# Environment — the Seed port of @term/face's `Environment`. In React it is the client-runtime wrapper: a provider
# stack (settings, query client, fonts, toast, layout-slot registry) around the responsive Layout, plus optional
# trailing hosts (Toast / ScrollRestoration / Scripts). In Seed the providers are not applicable (the reactive runtime
# has no React context tree, signals are imported directly, SSR is the dom native), so the meaningful piece is the
# viewport + Layout: Environment just wraps the page in Layout, which owns the viewport signal and the responsive
# three-section shell. The page fills Layout's middle `slot` through this one.

load @term/site/code/zone/render
  find element
load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append
load ./layout
  find layout

zone environment
  take host, like view
  zone layout
    slot
